  "created": "2026-05-07T11:46:30.483Z",
  "description": "A CLI tool for managing GitHub Projects and Copilot-assigned issues in bulk. Define your project in a YAML file and let orcai create issues, assign them to Copilot, and clean up when done.",
  "id": "OrcAI.Tool",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-05-07T11:50:08.907Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ZTeNDwHWRkWUsRC4D9ziNoQhMR8Z8YZaxWKMRcimwZDD2jJm9m1uY4KZFu9ooZIB3cyR/bke1b/m3V1uCBY0HQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 2802602,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/dburriss/orca",
  "published": "2026-05-07T11:46:30.483Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Brace expansion in glob patterns — `\"jobs/**/*.{yml,yaml}\"` now matches both `.yml` and `.yaml` files in a single invocation, for `orcai run` and `orcai validate`.\n`onClosedIssue` field in YAML job config and `--on-closed-issue` flag on `orcai run` — controls behaviour when a matching closed issue already exists. Valid values: `create` (default, creates a new issue), `reopen` (reopens the closed issue), `skip` (leaves the repo untouched), `fail` (exits with an error).\nRun summary and `--json` output now include `reopened` and `skipped` counts when `--on-closed-issue` is `reopen` or `skip`.\nGitHub write calls are now rate-limited with a token-bucket (default 60 writes/min) and automatically retried with exponential backoff on rate-limit errors (up to 3 retries, starting at 60s, doubling each time, capped at 5 min).\n`writesPerMinute` and `rateLimitRetries` config keys — override the rate-limit defaults in `~/.config/orcai/config.json` or `.orcai/config.json`.",
